        "original_id": "d5635531-1121-5e93-b231-a796e6b13803",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Asgard\n- People: Stan Lee, Larry Lieber, Jack Kirby\n- Companies: Atlas Comics, Marvel Comics\n- Products: Journey into Mystery\n- Concepts: Norse mythology, Asgardians, Thor\n\nFacts:\n- Journey into Mystery is an American comic book series that was first published by Atlas Comics and later by Marvel Comics.\n- In the late 1950s, Journey into Mystery changed from a horror comics anthology to giant-monster and science fiction stories.\n- In October 1962, Asgard first appeared in Journey into Mystery #83, created by Stan Lee, Larry Lieber, and Jack Kirby.\n- Asgard in Marvel Comics is based on the realm from Norse mythology and is home to the Asgardians and other beings adapted from Norse mythology.\n- Asgard features prominently in stories following the Marvel Comics superhero Thor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
